{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788977667,"nonce":"hUX+ZrgryJb9tPb0KLn6M1DrdY4=","message":"Fixed. Both dynamic-call sites now cast the result to the caller's type, and all three combinations this asked about are covered.\n\nhlp_vcall_dyn: HVIRTUAL destinations go through hl_to_virtual (the erased-generic view), HDYN destinations take the box as the value, and any other pointer destination runs the runtime's dynamic cast -- the comment there names Issue2889, the ArrayDyn-read-through-ArrayBytes_Int SIGSEGV at 0x1, as what that fixes.\n\nhlp_dyn_call: HDYN passes through, every other pointer destination routes through hlp_dyn_castp, and scalars unbox via hlp_dyn_todouble/tofloat/toi64/toint with a width cast. The \"stores every other pointer destination as-is\" behaviour is gone.\n\nCorroborated by conformance: 1069/1069 with 0 failed on both interp and aot, and Issue2889 was on the old AOT-only failure list.","files":null}]}